# Noony — Error Handling Rules

## Error Class Hierarchy

Import from `@noony-serverless/core`. Never throw generic `Error()`.

| Class | HTTP Status | When to use |
|-------|-------------|-------------|
| `ValidationError` | 400 | Invalid request body, query params, path params |
| `UnauthorizedError` | 401 | Missing or invalid authentication token |
| `ForbiddenError` | 403 | Authenticated but lacks permission |
| `NotFoundError` | 404 | Resource does not exist |
| `ConflictError` | 409 | Resource already exists, duplicate key |
| `InternalServerError` | 500 | Unexpected server-side failures |
| `HttpError` | custom | Base class — extend for custom status codes |
| `ServiceError` | n/a | Business logic errors in layers that don't know HTTP |

## Rules

### Always throw typed errors
```typescript
// WRONG
throw new Error('User not found');

// CORRECT
throw new NotFoundError('User not found');
```

### Never manually set status
```typescript
// WRONG — bypasses error formatting and logging
context.res.status(404).json({ error: 'Not found' });

// CORRECT — ErrorHandlerMiddleware formats the response
throw new NotFoundError('User not found');
```

### Wrap external API errors with cause chaining
```typescript
// WRONG — original stack lost
try {
  await externalApi.call();
} catch (err) {
  throw new InternalServerError('API failed');
}

// CORRECT — original error preserved as cause
try {
  await externalApi.call();
} catch (err) {
  throw new InternalServerError('API failed', err as Error);
}
```

### Use ServiceError in business logic layers
```typescript
// In a service class (doesn't know about HTTP)
if (!user) throw new ServiceError('USER_NOT_FOUND', 'User does not exist');

// In the handler (translates to HTTP)
try {
  return await userService.getUser(id);
} catch (err) {
  if (err instanceof ServiceError && err.code === 'USER_NOT_FOUND') {
    throw new NotFoundError(err.message);
  }
  throw new InternalServerError('Failed to get user', err as Error);
}
```

### Custom error classes
```typescript
export class PaymentRequiredError extends HttpError {
  constructor(message: string, cause?: Error) {
    super(402, message, cause);
  }
}
```

## Forbidden Patterns

- `throw new Error('...')` — becomes opaque 500 with no context
- `context.res.status(X).json(...)` — bypasses `ErrorHandlerMiddleware`
- `catch (err) { /* ignore */ }` — silent failures hide bugs
- Wrapping without cause: `new InternalServerError('msg')` when you have the original error
- `ErrorHandlerMiddleware` not at position 1 — errors from structural checks go uncaught

